---
import LegalLayout from '@/components/legal/LegalLayout.astro';
import DecisionNote from '@/components/legal/DecisionNote.astro';
import { site } from '@/data/site';

const sections = [
  { id: 'who', label: 'Who this is about' },
  { id: 'website', label: 'What this website does' },
  { id: 'enquiries', label: 'When you contact us' },
  { id: 'projects', label: 'Client project information' },
  { id: 'tools', label: 'Third-party tools' },
  { id: 'rights', label: 'Your choices and rights' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes to this policy' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  heading="Privacy policy"
  description="Draft privacy policy for SabiForge Digital, for owner and legal review. Not an approved document."
  document="privacy"
  sections={sections}
>
  <h2 id="who">1. Who this is about</h2>
  <p>
    This policy concerns the website of {site.name} and the information you share with the studio
    when you contact it. You can reach the studio at
    <a class="font-semibold underline" href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>
      {site.contact.email}
    </a>
    or on WhatsApp at {site.contact.whatsappDisplay}.
  </p>
  <DecisionNote id="P1" />
  <DecisionNote id="P2" />

  <h2 id="website">2. What this website does</h2>
  <p>These statements were checked against the website’s code at the time of drafting:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The website is a set of static pages. It has no user accounts, logins or payments.</li>
    <li>It sets no cookies and stores nothing in your browser’s local storage.</li>
    <li>It runs no analytics, advertising or tracking scripts.</li>
    <li>
      Fonts and images are served from the site itself. Pages make no requests to third-party
      services while you read them.
    </li>
    <li>
      The project brief builder on the contact page runs entirely in your browser. It does not send
      what you type to the studio or to any server.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These statements stop being true if a tool is added later. They must be re-checked before every
    launch.
  </p>
  <DecisionNote id="P7" />

  <h2 id="enquiries">3. When you contact us</h2>
  <p>
    The brief builder helps you prepare a message. To send it you choose one of three actions: open
    it in your email app, open it in WhatsApp, or copy it. Sending is your action.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      If you use email or WhatsApp, the message is handled by your email provider or by WhatsApp and
      then received by the studio. Those services have their own privacy policies.
    </li>
    <li>
      The studio receives what you choose to include, which may be your name, email address,
      business details and project description.
    </li>
    <li>If you call or message the studio directly, it receives your number and what you say.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>
      How the studio uses it, how long it keeps it, and whether it is shared are not yet decided.
    </strong>
  </p>
  <DecisionNote id="P3" />
  <DecisionNote id="P8" />
  <DecisionNote id="P9" />

  <h2 id="projects">4. Client project information</h2>
  <p>
    Working on a project involves receiving client information, such as content, product data,
    customer lists and account access. The rules for storing, sharing and deleting it are not yet
    decided.
  </p>
  <DecisionNote id="P5" />

  <h2 id="tools">5. Third-party tools</h2>
  <p>
    Today the website itself uses no third-party tools that run in your browser. The studio uses
    email and WhatsApp to communicate. Any hosting, analytics, form, CRM, scheduling or payment tool
    added later must be listed here.
  </p>
  <DecisionNote id="P6" />

  <h2 id="rights">6. Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can choose not to use the brief builder and to contact the studio in another way. The rights
    you have over your information, the law that applies, and how to exercise them have not yet been
    confirmed.
  </p>
  <DecisionNote id="P4" />
  <DecisionNote id="P10" />
  <DecisionNote id="P11" />

  <h2 id="changes">7. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    Once approved, the policy should show a version and date. This draft is version 0.1 of 6
    November 2026.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
